   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to maternal depression\ntreatment; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2017, amending the public\nhealth law, relating to maternal depression treatment, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 4000 and A. 8308, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7409",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7409-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 38,
       "fullName": "David Carlucci",
       "imgName": "370_david_carlucci.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 370,
       "sessionMemberId": 1072,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "CARLUCCI"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2500-k, Pub Health L; amd §2, Chap of 2017 (as proposed in S. 4000 and A. 8308)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7409\n\nSPONSOR: KRUEGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public health law, in relation to\nmaternal depression treatment; and to amend a chapter of the laws of\n2017, amending the public health law, relating to maternal depression\ntreatment, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 4000 and A. 8308,\nin relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo increase awareness among medical providers and about maternal\ndepression and provide information to the public on supports and treat-\nment for maternal depression.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 makes conforming amendments to chapter 463 of the laws of 2017\nby requiring the Department of Health and the Office of Mental Health,\nto provide information on how to locate providers who offer treatment\nand supports for maternal depression. This section also requires the\nDepartment of Health to inform healthcare providers of the need to raise\nawareness about maternal depression,\n\nSection 2 makes technical amendments to section 2 of chapter 463 of the\nlaws of 2017 by providing an effective date of June 30, 2018.\n\nSection 3 provides an immediate effective date, except that section 1\nshall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as chapter 463\nof the laws of 2017.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nSection 2500-k of the public health law requires the Commissioners to\nmake maternal depression information available to maternal health care\nproviders.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMaternal depression can lead to significant negative consequences for\nthose affected and their children and families. Mothers experiencing\nmaternal depression can have trouble caring for their new baby, be\nunable to work or look for work. This depression can also negatively\nimpact the essential growth and development of families and young chil-\ndren. Fortunately, treatment or maternal depression is successful for\n80-90% of patients and offers long-term health costs savings.  Given the\nefficacy of treatment, the State must ensure that medical practitioners\nand the public are informed about available resources to treat this\ndebilitating condition.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNegotiated chapter amendment to chapter 463 of the laws of 2017.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that section\none of this act shall take effect on June 30, 2018.\n",
